From: RV32 OP-TEE bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] lib: utils: mpxy: reqfwd: count the status word in the TEE response length

When the TEE domain has no more forwarded messages, the REQFWD driver
exits the domain from inside the RETRIEVE ecall. The return value of that
ecall is delivered to the resumed caller of the TEE channel, so it is the
TEE_COMMUNICATE response length seen by the supervisor. reqfwd->ack_len
holds only the register payload the OP-TEE transform wrote after the
4-byte RPMI status word, so the supervisor received one register too few.
On RV64 only the upper half of a3 is lost, which the OP-TEE UID check does
not notice. On RV32 a3 arrives as zero and the OP-TEE driver fails with
"api uid mismatch".

--- a/lib/utils/mpxy/fdt_mpxy_rpmi_reqfwd.c
+++ b/lib/utils/mpxy/fdt_mpxy_rpmi_reqfwd.c
@@ -256,7 +256,18 @@
 				dispatcher = mpxy_tee_get_dispatcher(tee_channel);
 				if (dispatcher && dispatcher->ops &&
 				    dispatcher->ops->domain_exit) {
-					*ack_len = reqfwd->ack_len;
+					/*
+					 * This ecall's return value lands in
+					 * the resumed TEE channel caller as the
+					 * TEE_COMMUNICATE response length. The
+					 * transform only counted the register
+					 * payload it wrote after the status
+					 * word, so add the status word here.
+					 * Without it the caller gets one
+					 * register less (a3 = 0 on RV32).
+					 */
+					*ack_len = reqfwd->ack_len ?
+						   reqfwd->ack_len + sizeof(u32) : 0;
 					reqfwd->ack_len = 0;
 					/* TEE use case: save state before domain_exit */
 					reqfwd->is_waiting_message = true;
